A||||14||gt2437||17" wheels -- how wide can you go???||||7||
Z||000000||gt2437||08-11-2001||10:50 PM||||Ok i sold the 17" x 7"s  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> moment of silence.... <IMG SRC="http://www.mumz.org/fiero.jpg"> <P>They were 38mm offset and i ran 225/45/17's all the way around.<P>Now I know 17" x 7.5" will fit in the front, and 17" x 9" will fit in the rear.... Does anyone know the offset that I would need?<P>I plan to run 225(215)/45/17's in the front and 275/40/17's in the rear.  <P>The Dvlish black GT (fiero shop ads) had those tires and rims sizes... TIA<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1486717&a=11524521&p=47383883&f=0" TARGET=_blank>1986 Pontiac Fiero GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1486717&a=11204369&f=0" TARGET=_blank>2000 VW 1.8T NB</A>||||reg||7
Z||000001||Primaris||08-12-2001||12:36 AM||||Why did you sell the 17 x 7's?  I was just looking at a bunch of 17 x 7 and am thinking about getting them in the future.  Did you have any problems or rubbing?<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
Z||000002||LT1 Chop Top||08-12-2001||12:51 AM||||I have 255-40-17 rear.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LT1 Chop Top||08-12-2001||12:52 AM||||Whoops, wheels are 17x9.  275/40/17's in the rear would be awesome!||||reg||14
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||08-12-2001||02:39 AM||||Does your car have coilovers on all 4 corners like the "Devilish" car does?||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||08-12-2001||05:39 AM||||17x7 (with 215/45/17) is all the larger I would go in front, there's no need.<P>In the rear, 17x8 will fit an 88 car with 245/40/17 withought rubbing.    17x9 and larger tyres will require coilovers.  275 is a bit big even for an 9" wheel, I'd recomend 265 or 255 (or a 10" wheel!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>in pre-88 cars, you'll need coilovers for anything larger than 7" in the rear imo.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000006||LT1 Chop Top||08-12-2001||06:10 AM||||Pontiaddict,<P>Rear has coil overs, front has drop spindles w/ AVO 12 position adjustable shocks.<P>What is the "devilish" car??||||reg||1
Z||000007||banditbalz||08-12-2001||04:31 PM||||LT1, this is the Devlish car...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bigwinner.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/uyih.jpg"> <P>used to be a 3.1 turbo but I believe the FieroShop has a new exotic engine setup. That's all I can say!<P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||08-12-2001||11:51 PM||||The car it should have been from the start (all I can say :)<P>Mmmm!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||Formula88||08-12-2001||11:58 PM||||Quoting from the West Coast Fiero's FAQ:<P>"We have experienced the maximum wheel and tire on the front<BR>            of a Fiero as 17 x 8 with a 45mm offset.  This car has 235x40x17<BR>            tires.  This wheel just touches the lower A-arm in maximum turning<BR>            and the tire just misses the top of inner fender well at maximum<BR>            up-wheel travel.  This combination keeps the tire inside the front<BR>            wheel well.<BR>            On the rear,  we have experienced 17 x 9 with a 45mm offset. This<BR>            car has 255x40x17 tires.  This diameter of the wheel is needed to<BR>            clear the upright on the rear suspension.  16 inch wheels will not<BR>            clear at 9 inches in width.  This combination will keep the tire <BR>            inside the rear wheel well."<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||gt2437||08-13-2001||01:45 AM||||Wow, thanks for the replies!<P>Primaris:  <BR>I happened to come across a deal I couldn't pass up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I had no problems at all with them.  I used to run 215/45/17 tires in the front and 235/45/17's in the rear, which looked better.  I got the 225's all the way around thinking I would put them on my VW, but they didn't look right.  That and i picked up the TT rims at a great price  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>225/45/17's did rub ever so slightly in the front though with the wheel fully turned.<P>Pontiaddict:<BR>Currently I have lowering springs from the Fiero store (Fall '98). Much more than the advertised 1" drop -- more like 2.5".  I will be getting coilovers & drop spindles soon though.<P>artherd:  <BR>why do you recommend coilovers for anything over 7" in width?  TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>banditbalz:<BR>Thanks for the sweet pics!<P>Formula88: <BR>Thanks for the tech numbers from West Coast Fieros  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  time to go shopping  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1486717&a=11524521&p=47383883&f=0" TARGET=_blank>1986 Pontiac Fiero GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1486717&a=11204369&f=0" TARGET=_blank>2000 VW 1.8T NB</A>||||reg||14
Z||000011||Pontiaddict||08-13-2001||02:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt2437:<BR><B>Wow, thanks for the replies!<P>Pontiaddict:<BR>Currently I have lowering springs from the Fiero store (Fall '98). Much more than the advertised 1" drop -- more like 2.5".  I will be getting coilovers & drop spindles soon though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know what you mean about the Fiero Store Springs.<P><BR>Formula88, is that info for all years, just 88, or pre 88?||||reg||1
Z||000012||artherd||08-13-2001||07:12 AM||||Hi gt2437, actually I only recomend <BR>coilovers for any wheel over 8" in width (read: 9" wheels and above :)<P>Though my expierence is pretty much limited to 88 cars, as all my fieros are 88s :)<P>Are you going to use wheels off an Audi TT? Are they also 5x100m? cool if so, want to know more about what you have in store!!<P>Best!!!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by gt2437:<BR><B>Wow, thanks for the replies!<BR>artherd:  <BR>why do you recommend coilovers for anything over 7" in width?  TIA  :) <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||Formula88||08-13-2001||11:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pontiaddict:<BR><B> I know what you mean about the Fiero Store Springs.<P><BR>Formula88, is that info for all years, just 88, or pre 88?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>According to an email I rec'd from Chris West asking this very question, it should be fine for all years.  My concern was the front wheels sticking out on an 88 with the same offset as the rear wheels, but he said it wouldn't be a problem.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||gt2437||08-13-2001||04:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Are you going to use wheels off an Audi TT? Are they also 5x100m? cool if so, want to know more about what you have in store!!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks artherd!<P>I am going to try out the TT Rims on the Fiero GT and see how they work.  They should look great in the back, however I'm pretty sure the 7.5" width and 32mm offset won't work to well in the front.  See sig for pics of the Audi TT 5 spoke polished rims (on VW).  I might run the stock VW rims (16x6.5", 35mm offset w/ 205/55/16) on the Fiero for the time being.<BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=1486717&a=11524521&p=47383883&f=0" TARGET=_blank>1986 Pontiac Fiero GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=1486717&a=11204369&f=0" TARGET=_blank>2000 VW 1.8T NB</A>||||reg||1
